  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Yard Crew's Flyer, Calmed Down",
    "overview": "Ellie's calm band style (`~/.claude/skills/pitch-site/references/calm-photo-style.md`) applied to a trades outfit. The page is a stack of full-width colour bands: off-white paper, slate navy and deep navy with faint diagonal lines. One warm accent, machine amber, comes from the trade (excavators, safety gear). The client has no logo or colours, so the TD mark is a navy tile with an amber ground line. Density is low and type is large. Every interactive path ends at the phone number or the quote form.\n\nPhotos are **generated examples of each service, not the client's jobs.** The alt text starts with \"Example:\" and the cards carry no captions that claim otherwise. Swap them for real photos once the owner sends some (provenance is in `HANDOFF.md`).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Full-width bands that alternate paper, navy and deep navy. No boxed sections.",
      "Amber is used as a fill only. When it has to be text on a light ground, it darkens to amber-ink.",
      "Cal Sans at weight 400 for every heading, label, button and the big phone number. System sans for running text.",
      "Flat surfaces. The only shadow belongs to the floating text circle.",
      "Motion is limited to the hero H1 letter bounce-in and one 12px fade-up for content below the first screen."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Amber-Is-Fill Rule",
        "body": "Amber (#f2a93b) never sets text on a light ground. On light grounds it becomes amber-ink (#8a5200). Text sitting on amber is ink (#12263a).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dark-Band Accent Rule",
        "body": "A heading's closing phrase goes amber (`.accent`) only on hero, navy or deep bands. Paper-band headings stay all ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Focus Rule",
        "body": "On light grounds focus is focus-blue (#1f5fa8), which keeps it distinct from the amber fills. On navy, deep, hero and footer grounds the focus outline switches to amber. The outline is 3px with a 3px offset.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One-Weight Display Rule",
        "body": "Cal Sans is only ever set at weight 400. Hierarchy comes from size alone, never from bold.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Nothing rests on a shadow except the fixed floating circle, because it is the only thing that sits above the page.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Texture-Means-Deep Rule",
        "body": "The line texture appears on deep navy grounds only: hero, how-it-works and footer. It never appears on slate navy or paper.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep amber as a fill with ink text on it, and use amber-ink (#8a5200) when amber has to be text on paper.",
      "**Do** build new sections as full-width bands from the paper, slate navy and deep-navy-with-texture set, with 64/96px padding.",
      "**Do** make list-like actions whole-row links, with hover limited to the arrow circle.",
      "**Do** keep every tap target at least 44px (buttons 56px, chips 48px).",
      "**Do** label generated photos as examples in their alt text until the owner sends real job photos.",
      "**Do** keep content visible at rest. Motion may only hide what starts below the first screen, and only when JS is running and reduced motion is off."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add hover backgrounds, shadows or outlines to service rows.",
      "**Don't** put shadows on cards, buttons or bands. The float is the only lifted element.",
      "**Don't** set Cal Sans in bold, or headings in the system face.",
      "**Don't** replace the floating circle with a sticky bottom bar.",
      "**Don't** publish the hidden unverified claims, or present the generated photos as the crew's own work."
    ]
  }
}